  "question": {
    "text": "In a mixture, two enantioners are found to be present in 85\\% and $15 \\%$ respectively. The enantiomeric. excess (ee) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$85 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$15 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$70 \\%$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$60 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$15 \\%$ will form racemic mixture with another $15 \\%$. Hence. the enantiomeric excess is $=(85-15)=70 \\%$"
  }
